course: dictionary
lesson: 11416
title: Getting used to it
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: When you do something again and again, it stops feeling strange. You become accustomed to it. Accustomed means used to something, so it feels normal. «Sam was not accustomed to the cold, so his fingers ached on the first morning.» By the end of the week the cold felt ordinary, because he had become accustomed to it.
explain: Accustomed almost always comes with to: be accustomed to, get accustomed to, grow accustomed to. The word after to is a thing or an action: «She grew accustomed to the noise of the busy city.» «He is accustomed to waking early» uses an -ing verb after to, so the action is waking.
explain: Accustomed can also mean usual or regular, as in «her accustomed seat by the window». Here it means the seat she always sits in. To check your meaning, swap in "usual" or "used to" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Accustomed is an adjective, and it is most often used in the phrase accustomed to.
fact: «Accustomed to» means used to something, so it feels normal.
fact: Phrases to learn: be accustomed to, get accustomed to, grow accustomed to, become accustomed to.
fact: «Accustomed» can also mean usual or regular, as in «his accustomed place».
fact: The word after to can be a noun, like «the heat», or an -ing verb, like «doing».
exercise: «After a month at the new school, Ana was accustomed to the long bus ride.» What does accustomed mean here? | Very tired of it | *Used to it, so it feels normal | Lost on the way | Angry about it
exercise: «Grandma's accustomed seat was by the fire.» What does accustomed mean here? | *Usual, the seat she always sat in | Broken and old | Brand new | Wet from the rain
exercise: Which word completes the sentence? «Lily will soon get ___ to her new home.» | careless | hungry | *accustomed | sleepy
test: «The fox was accustomed to hiding from hunters, so it stayed very still.» What does accustomed mean in this sentence? | Afraid of everything | *Used to it, so it hid often | Lost in the forest | Happy to be seen
test: «Ben is still not accustomed to his new glasses, but he is getting there.» What does "not accustomed to" mean here? | Able to see the moon | *Not yet used to them | Very pleased with them | Always wearing them
exam: «My accustomed route to school goes past the park, but today the gate was shut.» What does accustomed mean here? | Secret and hidden | *Usual, the way she always goes | Dangerous and new | Empty and quiet
